  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree with NNN nodes where the nodes are numbered from 111 to NNN. The tree is rooted at node 111.\n\nThe shortest distance between two nodes uuu and vvv is the number of edges in the unique shortest path between uuu and vvv in the tree. Let it be denoted by dist(u,v)\\text{dist}(u, v)dist(u,v).\n\nYou have QQQ queries of the following type:\n\nFor the iii-th query, let AiA_iAi​ be a set of KiK_iKi​ nodes in the tree denoted by Ai,1,Ai,2,⋯ ,Ai,KiA_{i, 1}, A_{i, 2}, \\cdots, A_{i, K_i}Ai,1​,Ai,2​,⋯,Ai,Ki​​.\n\nWe define the Ugliness of a node xxx as max(dist(x,y))\\text{max(dist} (x, y))max(dist(x,y)) over all y∈Aiy \\in A_iy∈Ai​.\n\nFor each query, find the minimum Ugliness among all nodes of the tree.\n\n**Note: Due to heavy input and output files, please use Fast IO.**\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ, denoting the number of nodes in the tree and the number of queries, respectively.\nThe next N−1N - 1N−1 lines describe the edges. The iii-th of these N−1N - 1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\nThen the QQQ queries follow. Each query consists of 222 lines of input.\n\nThe first line of the iii-th query contains a single integer KiK_iKi​, denoting the size of the set AiA_iAi​.\nThe second line of the iii-th query contains KiK_iKi​ space-separated integers Ai,1,Ai,2,⋯ ,Ai,KiA_{i, 1}, A_{i, 2}, \\cdots, A_{i, K_i}Ai,1​,Ai,2​,⋯,Ai,Ki​​, denoting the set of nodes in AiA_iAi​.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, print QQQ lines.\nThe iii-th line for each test case should print the answer for the iii-th query of that test case.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N,Q≤1051 \\leq N, Q \\leq 10^51≤N,Q≤105",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "The graph formed is a tree",
      "1≤Ki≤N1 \\leq K_i \\leq N1≤Ki​≤N",
      "1≤Ai,j≤N1 \\leq A_{i, j} \\leq N1≤Ai,j​≤N",
      "All elements in AiA_iAi​ are distinct",
      "The sum of NNN and QQQ over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105",
      "The sum of KiK_iKi​ over all test cases won't exceed 4⋅1054 \\cdot 10^54⋅105."
    ],
